---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS, GA4_ID, CLARITY_ID, CONSENT_MODE } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { label } from '../../i18n/nav';
import { facts } from '../../lib/facts';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const F = facts(lang);
const updated = displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS[lang]);
const tools = [GA4_ID && 'Google Analytics 4', CLARITY_ID && 'Microsoft Clarity'].filter(Boolean).join(' and ');
const optIn = CONSENT_MODE === 'opt-in';
const title = `Cookies ${F.year}: No Tracking Cookies on This Salary Site`;
const description = `In ${F.year} this site stores no tracking cookies and runs no audience measurement or ads. What the planned consent banner would change, and how to check yourself.`;
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} noindex={true}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: label('home', lang), path: route('home', lang) }, { name: label('cookies', lang), path: route('cookies', lang) }])]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: label('cookies', lang) }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies and similar technologies</h1>
    <p class="lead">This page completes the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. {tools ? `The site uses ${tools} only if you accept it.` : 'The short answer: today the site stores no cookies at all on your device.'}</p>

    <h2>The situation today</h2>
    {tools ? (
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies:</strong> none. The calculators work without them.</li>
        <li><strong>Audience measurement:</strong> {tools}, loaded {optIn ? 'only after you click “accept” in the consent banner' : 'with prior notice and the option to refuse at any time'}.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising cookies:</strong> none.</li>
        <li><strong>Browser storage:</strong> only your choice in the consent banner, so that we do not ask on every page. It is not a cookie and never leaves your device.</li>
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies:</strong> none. The calculators work without them.</li>
        <li><strong>Audience measurement:</strong> none. We use neither Google Analytics nor Microsoft Clarity nor any other tool.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising cookies:</strong> none. The site shows no ads.</li>
        <li><strong>Browser storage (localStorage, sessionStorage):</strong> the calculators do not use it. Your figures are not even stored locally.</li>
      </ul>
    )}
    {!tools && <p>That is why you see no consent banner: there is nothing to consent to. The widget embedded on other sites behaves the same way and stores nothing either.</p>}

    <h2>What about the link with my result?</h2>
    <p>After you change a field, the calculator writes the values into the page address so you can share the calculation. That is not a cookie: nothing stays on your device beyond ordinary browsing history, and the link only carries your figures if you copy it and send it yourself.</p>

    <h2>How to check for yourself</h2>
    <p>In Chrome, Edge or Firefox, open the developer tools (F12), go to the “Application” or “Storage” tab and choose “Cookies” for this domain. {tools ? 'Before you accept, the list is empty.' : 'The list is empty.'} The “Network” tab will also show that the page contacts no analytics or advertising servers{tools ? ' before your consent' : ''}.</p>

    <h2>If this changes</h2>
    <p>If we ever add audience measurement, we will first update this page and the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>, describing each cookie, its purpose and its lifetime. {optIn ? 'The site is set up so that tools requiring consent start only after you click “accept” in a banner where refusing is just as easy, and you can withdraw that choice at any time.' : 'You will be able to switch them off at any time.'}</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Version of {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
